  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wet wipes production in the Palestinian Territories</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Currently, all wet wipes are imported into Palestine from Israel. The partners would like to establish a production facility for wet wipes in flow packs for baby and personal use. The facility will market its products in the Palestinian Territories, Jordan and Iraq and it will acquire the certificates to export to the US and Europe in a later stage. The facility will have their own research lab where the partner will develop the lotions.The applicant, the Jordanian company ALSAAD Hygienic Paper Co., is a manufacturer and distributor of hygienic paper products in Jordan and neighbouring countries.The local partner is Munir J. Kort. He will be the general manager of the facility.The third partner is the company George Garabidian Co., a company specialising in customised group tours and pilgrimages to the Holy Land. The family of George Garabidian &amp; Co. owned and operated TAKO Hygienic Paper Company, the only hygienic paper company in the West Bank that operated from 1964 to 2001.The third partner is located in East Jerusalem.The three partners will set up a joint venture for this project in Jericho, the Palestinian Territories.</narrative>
  </description>
